{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_14-15-46-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft; python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nimport json\np='update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd['investigations'].append({\n  \\\"ref\\\":\\\"@verify_stale_read_basis\\\",\n  \\\"question\\\":\\\"Under per-node timers, does the cut-off leader's successful confirmation coexist with committed state that has already moved past what that leader has applied, so that a caller following the documented read pattern would rest a read on a state the cluster has left behind?\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"raft_verifyleader_votes\\\",\\\"raft_quorumsize_voters\\\",\\\"replication_notifyall\\\",\\\"config_validate_timer_relations\\\",\\\"raft_follower_election_trigger\\\"],\n  \\\"hypothesis\\\":\\\"If the confirmation window overlaps a competing leader's election, it also overlaps that leader's first commit: the new leader can append and commit within a round trip of in-memory RPCs, while the cut-off leader keeps confirming against the nonvoter's acknowledgement until its lease expires, so confirmations and an advanced committed index should coexist.\\\",\n  \\\"discriminator\\\":\\\"Repeat the mixed-timer trial and the uniform control, and inside each confirmation poll also compare the competing leader's commit index with the cut-off leader's applied index. The mixed case should show confirmations while the competing leader's commit index is above the cut-off leader's applied index; the control should never elect a competing leader at all, so the comparison cannot be satisfied there.\\\",\n  \\\"disposition\\\":\\\"active\\\",\n  \\\"parent_id\\\":\\\"92e710d02abc4842a2f6c79e3aae70e4-question-0\\\"\n})\nd['experiment']={\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"@verify_stale_read_basis\\\",\n  \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"raft_verifyleader_votes\\\",\\\"raft_quorumsize_voters\\\",\\\"replication_notifyall\\\",\\\"config_validate_timer_relations\\\",\\\"raft_follower_election_trigger\\\"],\n  \\\"scope\\\":{\n    \\\"description\\\":\\\"Fourteen trials on hand-built four-node clusters, one per trial: twelve with per-node timers (the leader carrying 50ms heartbeat, election and lease; the other nodes 10ms heartbeat, 20ms election, 5ms lease) and two with every node on the leader's settings. Each trial forces leadership onto the slow node, demotes one node to nonvoter, isolates the leader and that nonvoter from the two remaining voters in both directions, and then, while polling the verification path, has the first competing leader to appear commit one entry and compares that leader's commit index with the cut-off leader's applied index on every confirmation obtained.\\\",\n    \\\"assumptions\\\":[\n      \\\"Per-node configurations are legal because ValidateConfig validates each node on its own; the mixed case represents a cluster whose members do not share timers.\\\",\n      \\\"The entry committed by the new leader is submitted through the exported Apply API and its future is waited on with a bound before the commit index is read.\\\",\n      \\\"The cut-off leader's applied index and the competing leader's commit index are read from the same runtime objects the verification uses.\\\",\n      \\\"Verification is driven through the same channel the exported API uses.\\\",\n      \\\"The dry run is native feedback only; the retained execution is what will be interpreted.\\\"\n    ],\n    \\\"excluded\\\":[\n      \\\"No application read is served, so what is measured is the coexistence of a confirmation with an advanced committed index, not a value handed to a client.\\\",\n      \\\"No on-disk store, no network transport and no multi-process execution.\\\",\n      \\\"Only one timer pair is contrasted.\\\"\n    ],\n    \\\"parameters\\\":{\n      \\\"trials\\\":\\\"12 mixed (trial ids 0-11), 2 uniform controls (trial ids 12-13)\\\",\n      \\\"poll_interval_ms\\\":2,\n      \\\"recorded_operands\\\":\\\"leader_lease_ms, voter_election_ms, voter_election_shorter_than_lease, polls, confirmations, first_peer_leader_ms, confirmations_after_peer_leader, confirmation_after_peer_leader, peer_write_committed, commit_ahead_while_confirming, peer_commit_index_at_overlap, leader_applied_at_overlap, leader_applied_index, commit_ahead_ms\\\"\n    }\n  },\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"pre\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"verify_baseline\\\"}],\n  \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n    {\\\"event\\\":\\\"verify_exposure\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"trial\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"pre\\\",\n     \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"voter_election_shorter_than_lease\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True}],\n     \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"commit_ahead_while_confirming\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n     \\\"description\\\":\\\"In every mixed-timer trial at least one confirmation is obtained while the competing leader's commit index is already above the cut-off leader's applied index; a trial without one would be reported as a witness.\\\"},\n    {\\\"event\\\":\\\"verify_exposure\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"trial\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"pre\\\",\n     \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"voter_election_shorter_than_lease\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False}],\n     \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"commit_ahead_while_confirming\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n     \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: with every node on the leader's settings no competing leader is elected during the window, so no confirmation coincides with an advanced commit.\\\"}\n  ],\n  \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"Each trial is the mixed-timer harness with one addition: while the verification poll runs, the first of the two isolated nodes to report Leader has one entry applied through the exported API with a bounded wait, and every confirmation that follows also reads that leader's commit index and the cut-off leader's applied index, setting the overlap flag when the commit index is the larger. The harness reports one summary event per trial with the counts, the first competing leader's elapsed time, how many confirmations followed one, whether the competing leader committed the entry, whether any confirmation coincided with a commit index above the cut-off leader's applied index, and the two indexes and elapsed time at that moment. Only the TestAssurance-prefixed test is selected and no production file is modified.\\\"\n}\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),indent=2)\nprint('ok', [i.get('id') or i.get('ref') for i in d['investigations']])\nPYEOF\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_14-15-46-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
